# Cloudflare Pages routing for platform.solarkal.com
#
# /faropoint, /plymouthreit and so on are not real files. Every path serves
# client.html, which reads the slug from the URL and asks /api/data what the
# signed-in person is allowed to see.
#
# Status 200 (rewrite), not 301/302, so the pretty URL stays in the address bar.
#
# The Worker route on /api/* is evaluated before Pages, so it is not caught by
# this rule. Do not add a rule for /api here.
#
# This file must sit in the ROOT of the Pages deployment, next to client.html.

/*    /client    200
